      "url": "https://x.com/N01ennn/status/2093794050562551926",
      "text": "HOLY SHIT. MY GROK BOT BUILT A DROPSHIPPING COMPANY FOR $61\n\n$61 was the whole budget. Stack, first orders, everything.\n\nIt did not ask me for a store name. It named the floor itself. AISLE NINE. That is what shows up on every label that leaves the dock now.\n\nNine days in it is sitting on $2,180 and it has paid its own $60 stack twice.\n\nThe rule has not moved. I do not top it up. If the balance touches zero AISLE NINE is wiped and I do not rebuild it.\n\nFour ports feed four belts. Shopify, Temu, AliExpress, Alibaba. Every parcel has to survive six seats:\n\n> SOURCE only opens a port if the supplier shipped under four days on thirty straight orders\n> SCOUT copies four proven catalogs and refuses anything with more than eleven sellers on it\n> PRICE kills any SKU under $18 margin after fees and shipping\n> QC never picks, it only pulls from the line, and the pull is final\n> REFUND never argues, it pays out before the customer opens the chat\n> DISPATCH never picks, it only signs, and nothing leaves the dock unsigned\n\nDay four it was down to $11.40. I had the shutdown post half written.\n\nThen it did the thing nobody programmed.\n\nIt closed three of the four ports. Ran the entire floor through one supplier for thirty-one hours and listed nothing new. 214 products came across the board that day and it took none of them. Every store I follow was posting winning-product screenshots that afternoon and AISLE NINE sat there refusing.\n\nThe next morning it listed two SKUs.\n\nOne of them did 61 orders in nine hours at $40 a parcel. It swept the margin, paid the stack out of it, and went straight back to refusing things.\n\nIt did not learn to find winning products. It learned that most products are not worth listing.\n\nbookmark this",
      "original_text": "HOLY SHIT. MY GROK BOT BUILT A DROPSHIPPING COMPANY FOR $61\n\n$61 was the whole budget. Stack, first orders, everything.\n\nIt did not ask me for a store name. It named the floor itself. AISLE NINE. That is what shows up on every label that leaves the dock now.\n\nNine days in it is sitting on $2,180 and it has paid its own $60 stack twice.\n\nThe rule has not moved. I do not top it up. If the balance touches zero AISLE NINE is wiped and I do not rebuild it.\n\nFour ports feed four belts. Shopify, Temu, AliExpress, Alibaba. Every parcel has to survive six seats:\n\n> SOURCE only opens a port if the supplier shipped under four days on thirty straight orders\n> SCOUT copies four proven catalogs and refuses anything with more than eleven sellers on it\n> PRICE kills any SKU under $18 margin after fees and shipping\n> QC never picks, it only pulls from the line, and the pull is final\n> REFUND never argues, it pays out before the customer opens the chat\n> DISPATCH never picks, it only signs, and nothing leaves the dock unsigned\n\nDay four it was down to $11.40. I had the shutdown post half written.\n\nThen it did the thing nobody programmed.\n\nIt closed three of the four ports. Ran the entire floor through one supplier for thirty-one hours and listed nothing new. 214 products came across the board that day and it took none of them. Every store I follow was posting winning-product screenshots that afternoon and AISLE NINE sat there refusing.\n\nThe next morning it listed two SKUs.\n\nOne of them did 61 orders in nine hours at $40 a parcel. It swept the margin, paid the stack out of it, and went straight back to refusing things.\n\nIt did not learn to find winning products. It learned that most products are not worth listing.\n\nbookmark this",
      "links": [],
      "translation_zh": "卧槽。我的 GROK 机器人用 $61 搭建了一家代发货公司\n\n$61 就是全部预算。技术栈、首批订单，所有一切。\n\n它没有问我要店名。它自己给运营地板起了名。AISLE NINE。现在从码头发出的每个标签上显示的都是这个。\n\n第九天，它账上有 $2,180，而且已经两次支付了自己的 $60 技术栈费用。\n\n规则没有变。我不给它充值。如果余额归零，AISLE NINE 就会被清除，而我不会重建它。\n\n四个端口供给四条传送带。Shopify、Temu、AliExpress、Alibaba。每个包裹都必须通过六个席位：\n\n> SOURCE 只有在供应商连续三十个订单都在四天内发货时，才会打开一个端口\n> SCOUT 复制四个已经验证的目录，并拒绝任何有超过十一个卖家的商品\n> PRICE 会淘汰扣除费用和运费后利润低于 $18 的任何 SKU\n> QC 从不挑选，它只从线上抽走，且一旦抽走就是最终决定\n> REFUND 从不争辩，它会在客户打开聊天前就退款\n> DISPATCH 从不挑选，它只签收，未签收的东西一律不得离开码头\n\n第四天，它降到了 $11.40。我已经把关停帖子写了一半。\n\n然后它做了没人编程让它做的事。\n\n它关闭了四个端口中的三个。让整个运营地板通过一个供应商运行了三十一个小时，并且没有上架任何新品。那天有 214 个产品出现在看板上，它一个都没要。那天下午我关注的每家店都在发布爆款产品截图，而 AISLE NINE 就坐在那里拒绝。\n\n第二天早上，它上架了两个 SKU。\n\n其中一个在九小时内完成了 61 个订单，每个包裹 $40。它把利润一扫而空，用其中的钱支付了技术栈费用，然后立刻又回到拒绝东西的状态。\n\n它学会的不是寻找爆款产品。它学会的是大多数产品都不值得上架。\n\n收藏这条",
      "translation_status": "translated",
